Let an iPhone with ProMotion present above 60 frames a second.

An iPhone holds an app to 60 Hz unless Info.plist sets CADisableMinimumFrameDurationOnPhone;
the in-game settings' frame rate "Max" (pocket/translation/AppKit/PocketSettings.m) means the
screen's own rate, 120 Hz on ProMotion. Both Info.plists get it: launcher/Info.plist (the
TolkaraDiagnostics target, and tools/build_ios.py, which starts from it) and
authorization/App/Integrated-Info.plist (the Tolkara target). iPads and 60 Hz iPhones ignore it.
Upstream candidate: brand-free.

--- a/launcher/Info.plist
+++ b/launcher/Info.plist
@@ -4,6 +4,8 @@
 <dict>
 	<key>UIFileSharingEnabled</key>
 	<true/>
+	<key>CADisableMinimumFrameDurationOnPhone</key>
+	<true/>
 	<key>CFBundleVersion</key>
 	<string>$(CURRENT_PROJECT_VERSION)</string>
 	<key>CFBundleShortVersionString</key>
--- a/authorization/App/Integrated-Info.plist
+++ b/authorization/App/Integrated-Info.plist
@@ -4,6 +4,8 @@
 <dict>
 	<key>UIFileSharingEnabled</key>
 	<true/>
+	<key>CADisableMinimumFrameDurationOnPhone</key>
+	<true/>
 	<key>CFBundleShortVersionString</key>
 	<string>$(MARKETING_VERSION)</string>
 	<key>CFBundleVersion</key>
